; Time log {{year}}
;
; Clock in:   i DATE TIME ACCOUNT[  DESCRIPTION]
; Clock out:  o DATE TIME [ACCOUNT]
;
; Example (remove the leading ";" to use it):
; i {{year}}-03-14 09:00:00 work:project  what you are doing
; o {{year}}-03-14 10:30:00 work:project
;
; Sessions are matched by account. You can be clocked in to several accounts at once;
; a clock-out with no account closes the most recent clock-in.
; A session that crosses midnight is split by day. Times are your local clock time.
; Lines starting with ; # or * are comments.

; Time log {{year}}
;
; A day starts with a date. Under it, one line per account, then at least two
; spaces, then how long:
;
;   {{year}}-03-14
;   work:programming  .... ....     each dot is 15 minutes; spaces only group them
;   work:research     1.5            a plain number is hours
;   personal:reading  45m            units: s m h d w mo y (no space after the number)
;   work:admin        ccecces        letters: 15 minutes each, counted per letter (a type)
;
; An account with no amount counts as 0. Lines starting with ; or # are comments.

; Time by type
;
; Each letter is 15 minutes and counts as a type, so one line can be split
; by kind of work. Pick your own letters, for example:
;   c = coding   r = review   m = meetings   e = email
;
;   {{year}}-03-14
;   work:project-a  ccccrrm      (1h coding, 30m review, 15m meetings)
;
; Wedger totals each letter separately. Delete these comments when you like.
